":"`compile` resolves MLIR backend binary from `CIM_MLIR_COMPILER_BIN` if set; otherwise it uses the default project build output (`build/bin/main`)."},"311":{"id":"/docs/Compiler/DSL-and-MLIR-Backend-51","page_id":"/docs/Compiler/DSL-and-MLIR-Backend","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Compiler/DSL-and-MLIR-Backend#relationship-with-op-level","content":"During OP-level compilation, certain operators — particularly depthwise convolution and fallback convolution paths — need custom ISA code beyond basic lowering rules. In these cases, OP-level invokes this same DSL-to-ISA pipeline to compile the kernel. The resulting instruction blocks are then inserted into the global per-core ISA file alongside the instructions produced by direct lowering."},"312":{"id":"/docs/Compiler/DSL-and-MLIR-Backend-52","page_id":"/docs/Compiler/DSL-and-MLIR-Backend","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Compiler/DSL-and-MLIR-Backend#relationship-with-op-level","content":"This invocation is transparent: users do not provide DSL source to OP-level. The kernel templates are generated internally, compiled through the pass pipeline above, and merged into the final output."},"313":{"id":"/docs/Compiler/OP-Level","page_id":"/docs/Compiler/OP-Level","type":"page","content":"OP-Level","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Compiler","Internals"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/Compiler/OP-Level"},"314":{"id":"/docs/Compiler/OP-Level-0","page_id":"/docs/Compiler/OP-Level","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Compiler/OP-Level","content":"Lower CG tasks to per-core ISA with synchronization and code assembly"},"315":{"id":"/docs/Compiler/OP-Level-1","page_id":"/docs/Compiler/OP-Level","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Compiler/OP-Level#op-level-processing-steps","content":"OP-Level Processing Steps"},"316":{"id":"/docs/Compiler/OP-Level-2","page_id":"/docs/Compiler/OP-Level","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Compiler/OP-Level#parse-cg-tasks-toc","content":"Parse CG Tasks [!toc]"},"317":{"id":"/docs/Compil