eparate phase offsets within each cycle, allowing instruction decode and issue to be pipelined."},"1454":{"id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model-16","page_id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model#per-cycle-progress-rules","content":"Each cycle, the core independently evaluates decode, issue, and PC advancement."},"1455":{"id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model-17","page_id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model#issue","content":"At each issue point, `processIssue` broadcasts a payload to all execute units. Only the matched unit type receives a non-null payload — all others receive `nullptr`."},"1456":{"id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model-18","page_id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model#stall-and-conflict-arbitration","content":"The core stalls when either condition holds:"},"1457":{"id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model-19","page_id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model#stall-and-conflict-arbitration","content":"The instruction stream has been fully decoded (`id_finish` is true)"},"1458":{"id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model-20","page_id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model#stall-and-conflict-arbitration","content":"Any execute-unit conflict signal is true"},"1459":{"id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model-21","page_id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model#stall-and-conflict-arbitration","content":"Each unit has a `ConflictHandler` that checks whether its currently allocated resources (memory regions, data paths, functor configurations) overlap with those required by the incoming instruction."},"1460":{"id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model-22","page_id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model#stall-and-conflict-arbitration","content":"The following table lists the conflict dimensions checked during instruction scheduling."},"1461":{"id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model-23","page_id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model#stall-and-conflict-arbitration","content":"Dimension"},"1462":{"id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model-24","page_id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model#stall-and-conflict-arbitration","content":"Runtime Rule"},"1463":{"id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model-25","page_id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model#stall-and-conflict-arbitration","content":"Unit readiness"},"1464":{"id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model-26","page_id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model#stall-and-conflict-arbitration","content":"Same unit type stalls when target unit `ready == false`"},"1465":{"id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model-27","page_id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model#stall-and-conflict-arbitration","content":"Memory overlap"},"1466":{"id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model-28","page_id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model#stall-and-conflict-arbitration","content":"Conflict on `read/write/used` bitmap intersection"},"1467":{"id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model-29","page_id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model#stall-and-conflict-arbitration","content":"Data path"},"1468":{"id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model-30","page_id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model#stall-and-conflict-arbitration","content":"Conflict on same data path type or same dedicated data path ID"},"1469":{"id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model-31","page_id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model#stall-and-conflict-arbitration","content":"SIMD functor"},"1470":{"id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model-32","page_id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model#stall-and-conflict-arbitration","content":"Two SIMD instructions with different functor configs conflict"},"1471":{"id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model-33","page_id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model#stall-and-conflict-arbitration","content":"Reduce functor"},"1472":{"id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model-34","page_id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model#stall-and-conflict-arbitration","content":"Two Reduce instructions with different functor configs conflict"},"1473":{"id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model-35","page_id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model#stall-and-conflict-arbitration","content":"Decode/issue does not imply immediate execution.\nAn issued instruction waits until the target unit is ready and the enable signal is asserted before execution begins."},"1474":{"id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model-36","page_id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model#branch-and-jump","content":"Branch/jump condition and `pc_increment` are resolved during decode"},"1475":{"id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model-37","page_id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model#branch-and-jump","content":"No dedicated execute-unit operation is required for branch/jump decision"},"1476":{"id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model-38","page_id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model#branch-and-jump","content":"The ISA defines `TAG` as a synchronization point marker and `WAIT` as a pairwise synchronization primitive (see Inter-Core Synchronization for the architectural specification). In the current simulator runtime, these are implemented as follows:"},"1477":{"id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model-39","page_id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model#branch-and-jump","content":"Decoded as control opcodes but routed to `TransferUnit` for execution"},"1478":{"id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model-40","page_id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model#branch-and-jump","content":"`TAG` attaches a `sync_id` to the next `global_store`, enabling the receiver to track write completion"},"1479":{"id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model-41","page_id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model#branch-and-jump","content":"Consecutive `TAG` without an intervening tagged store is treated as a fatal invalid sequence"},"1480":{"id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model-42","page_id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model#branch-and-jump","content":"`WAIT` blocks until `expected_writes` tagged stores for the given `sync_id` have completed"},"1481":{"id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model-43","page_id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model#branch-and-jump","content":"`WAIT` payload contains `source_id`, but current completion logic is keyed by `sync_id` and `expected_writes`.\nDo not assume source-level filtering in current runtime behavior."},"1482":{"id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model-44","page_id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model#branch-and-jump","content":"Performs collective synchronization across multiple cores (see Inter-Core Synchronization). All participating cores must reach the barrier before any can proceed."},"1483":{"id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model-45","page_id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model#branch-and-jump","content":"Decoded as control opcode with `pc_increment = 1`"},"1484":{"id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model-46","page_id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model#branch-and-jump","content":"All cores specified by `num_cores` must reach the same `barrier_id` before execution continues"},"1485":{"id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model-47","page_id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model#timing-and-energy-accounting","content":"The simulator charges dynamic energy per-event during compute, memory, and network operations. Static energy comes from configured static power and total simulated runtime."},"1486":{"id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model-48","page_id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model#timing-and-energy-accounting","content":"Stall cycles produce no dynamic energy but extend the runtime, increasing static energy. Pipeline stalls from resource conflicts or synchronization waits affect the energy/performance tradeoff even though no useful work is performed."},"1487":{"id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model-49","page_id":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Simulator/Execution-Model#timing-and-energy-accounting","content":"For output format and metric definitions, see Output and Metrics."},"1488":{"id":"/docs/Simulator/Input-Files","page_id":"/docs/Simulator/Input-Files","type":"page","content":"Input Files","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Simulator","Inputs and Outputs"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/Simulator/Input-Files"},"1489":{"id":"/docs/Simulator/Input-Files-0","page_id":"/doc