","content":"The opcode bits `X` and `Y` control immediate offset addressing for source and destination:"},"1920":{"id":"/docs/Abstraction/Instruction-Design/Instruction-Set/Data-Movement-8","page_id":"/docs/Abstraction/Instruction-Design/Instruction-Set/Data-Movement","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Abstraction/Instruction-Design/Instruction-Set/Data-Movement#operation-flags","content":"The `MEM_CPY` instruction uses optional flags to enable offset addressing for source and/or destination addresses:"},"1921":{"id":"/docs/Abstraction/Instruction-Design/Instruction-Set/Data-Movement-9","page_id":"/docs/Abstraction/Instruction-Design/Instruction-Set/Data-Movement","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Abstraction/Instruction-Design/Instruction-Set/Data-Movement#operation-flags","content":"**Flag Combinations:**"},"1922":{"id":"/docs/Abstraction/Instruction-Design/Instruction-Set/Data-Movement-10","page_id":"/docs/Abstraction/Instruction-Design/Instruction-Set/Data-Movement","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Abstraction/Instruction-Design/Instruction-Set/Data-Movement#operation-flags","content":"Flags"},"1923":{"id":"/docs/Abstraction/Instruction-Design/Instruction-Set/Data-Movement-11","page_id":"/docs/Abstraction/Instruction-Design/Instruction-Set/Data-Movement","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Abstraction/Instruction-Design/Instruction-Set/Data-Movement#operation-flags","content":"Opcode"},"1924":{"id":"/docs/Abstraction/Instruction-Design/Instruction-Set/Data-Movement-12","page_id":"/docs/Abstraction/Instruction-Design/Instruction-Set/Data-Movement","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Abstraction/Instruction-Design/Instruction-Set/Data-Movement#operation-flags","content":"Source Address"},"1925":{"id":"/docs/Abstraction/Instruction-Design/Instruction-Set/Data-Movement-13","page_id":"/docs/Abstraction/Instruction-Design/Instruction-Set/Data-Movement","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Abstraction/Instruction-Design/Instruction-Set/Data-Movement#operati